  "solution": "Given:\n\nx + (1/x) = - 6\n\nFormula used:\n\nIf x + (1/x) = P, then\n\n⇒ x² + (1/x²) = (P² - 2) \n\nIf x + (1/x) = P, then\n\n⇒ x3 + (1/x3) = P3 - 3P\n\nx5 + (1/x5) = {x3 + (1/x3)} × {x2 + 1/x2} - {x + (1/x)}\n\nCalculation:\n\nx + (1/x) = - 6\n\n⇒ x2 + (1/x2) = (- 6)² - 2\n\n⇒ 36 - 2 = 34\n\nNow,\n\nx + (1/x) = - 6\n\n⇒ x3 + (1/x3) = (- 6)3 - 3 (- 6)\n\n⇒ (- 216) + 18 = (- 198)\n\nx5 + (1/x5) = {x3 + (1/x3)} × {x2 + 1/x2} - {x + (1/x)}\n\n⇒ (- 198) × 34 - (- 6)\n\n⇒ (- 6732) + 6 = - 6726\n\n**∴ The correct answer is - 6726.**",
